1
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

2
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,720
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

3
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

4
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:05,399
How about a glass of wine?

5
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:11,071
Sure, wine sounds nice.

6
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:13,031
All right.

7
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,128
You okay?

8
00:01:27,129 --> 00:01:30,048
Nothing in this house
seems to be cooperating today.

9
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,175
Here, let me.

10
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:37,514
It's not much,
but I'd like to be helpful somehow.

11
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,017
Then I'll leave it to you.

12
00:01:41,018 --> 00:01:42,144
Sure.

13
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:05,624
I should put on some music.

14
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,377
Is there anything you want to listen to?

15
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:10,797
Whatever you like.

16
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:29,274
I haven't listened to this in forever.

17
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,361
I used to listen to it all the time.

18
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,280
It might be a little scratchy.

19
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:38,033
Found it.

20
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:26,832
This feels like you, Jisun.

21
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:29,584
What makes you say that?

22
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:37,968
There's something lonely about you,
but it's kind of alluring.

23
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:07,497
Thank you.

24
00:04:44,743 --> 00:04:50,247
EPISODE 4
BOOMERANG

25
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:53,834
 <i>The phone is turned off.
Please leave a message after…</i>

26
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:55,337
Her phone's still off.

27
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,465
The principal is in
a meeting right now, so…

28
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:01,426
We're looking into it too.

29
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,469
All right, bye.

30
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:05,513
Where the heck is she?

31
00:05:05,514 --> 00:05:07,681
I have no idea. Her phone's off.

32
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:09,099
 Why is her phone off?

33
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:11,102
I'm not sure because it's turned off.

34
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:18,025
I mean, doesn't this just make it look
like she's the one they're talking about?

35
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:19,944
If it isn't her, she needs to say so.

36
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:22,614
Otherwise, how are we
supposed to figure out what to do?

37
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:25,157
How can she deny it?

38
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:27,660
We're the only private school
in Sangcheon--

39
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:29,203
You think I don't know that?

40
00:05:29,204 --> 00:05:32,541
We need to hear it from her directly
before we can take further action!

41
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:34,835
Sir…

42
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:38,128
Complaints are pouring in
on the school website

43
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,548
asking if Kang Jisun
is the gold-digger teacher.

44
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:42,758
IS KANG JISUN
THE GOLD-DIGGER TEACHER?

45
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:47,972
But who's the man?

46
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:51,726
Oh, hello, sir.

47
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,937
He's in a meeting right now.

48
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:56,648
I understand.

49
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:02,820
The head of the board wants you to call.

50
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:07,284
What the hell
does she take this school for?

51
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:12,163
Mr. Park, keep trying to reach Ms. Kang.

52
00:06:12,706 --> 00:06:14,999
And you arrange for someone
to cover her classes.

53
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,042
Sir.

54
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:20,462
Shouldn't we deal
with Ms. Kang's disciplinary action first?

55
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:23,299
The parents are going to start
showing up here soon.

56
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,467
Yes, I think that would be best too.

57
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:29,139
We need to take disciplinary action first
if we want things to settle down.

58
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:33,059
When does Ms. Kang's contract end?

59
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,231
Hey, Min Hyunsoo.

60
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:41,401
Ms. Kang reported
being sexually assaulted, right?

61
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:45,322
And your dad was at the police station
a few days ago over a sex offense.

62
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:48,825
You think maybe Ms. Kang
and your dad did it?

63
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,036
Shut up.

64
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:53,037
I never said they did.

65
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:54,705
I'm just asking.

66
00:06:54,706 --> 00:06:56,457
I said shut up.

67
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:58,001
Fine, man.

68
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:02,088
But if they really did it,
what about your mom?

69
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:04,215
Does she know?

70
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:09,136
I'm just asking, man!

71
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:10,138
Hey!

72
00:07:11,056 --> 00:07:12,139
Damn it.

73
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,392
Oh, my gosh! What are you two doing?

74
00:07:15,477 --> 00:07:16,935
What do you think you're doing?

75
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:20,230
Geez. I was just asking
about Ms. Kang and his dad.

76
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:21,649
Damn it.

77
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:23,193
-  Get lost!
- My goodness! Hey!

78
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:26,946
Hello, everyone.
Welcome to <i>Baek Hanui's Question Mark</i>.

79
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,948
It's an unusually warm spring day.

80
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:33,744
But did you know that weather like this
can actually put our hearts at risk?

81
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:37,039
Today, we're joined by
cardiovascular surgeon, Dr. Min Junho,

82
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:40,709
who's here to tell us how
to keep our hearts healthy.

83
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:42,378
BAEK HANUI'S QUESTION MARK

84
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:43,546
Welcome.

85
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:45,255
Dr. Min,

86
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:49,259
spring usually puts everyone
in high spirits,

87
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:51,720
but it can actually be dangerous
for our hearts?

88
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,263
Yes, that's right.

89
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:55,433
Spring is a season
of major temperature swings.

90
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,562
Yes.

91
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:02,731
Dr. Min.

92
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:07,111
You did a great job.
I learned a lot thanks to you.

93
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,655
You were great too.

94
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:12,742
If you're free for dinner,
would you like to join me?

95
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:15,787
What do you think?

96
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:19,082
Oh…

97
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:21,584
I wasn't expecting that.

98
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:28,799
If I take "unexpected" in a good way,
it means you were pleasantly surprised.

99
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,300
If I take it in a bad way,

100
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:32,637
it means you're getting ready
to turn me down, right?

101
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:38,727
There's something I haven't quite
sorted out emotionally,

102
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:43,147
so I don't really have the headspace
to spend time with someone right now.

103
00:08:43,148 --> 00:08:44,982
I heard you were single.

104
00:08:44,983 --> 00:08:47,235
Do you have a girlfriend?

105
00:08:49,154 --> 00:08:52,531
There was someone
I wanted a serious relationship with,

106
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:53,950
but it didn't work out.

107
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:57,579
How could anyone turn you down?

108
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,373
I just wish she'd recognize

109
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:03,877
how I truly feel, even at this point.

110
00:09:09,716 --> 00:09:11,593
I'm sorry.

111
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,803
That's too bad.

112
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,515
Next time we have you on,
make sure you've got it sorted out.

113
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:40,287
<i>The phone is turned off.
Please leave a message</i>…

114
00:09:41,456 --> 00:09:42,457
Jieun.

115
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,295
Did you see the article?

116
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,297
Yeah.

117
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:54,928
Are you okay?

118
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:59,182
Jisun's not answering her phone?

119
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:02,560
No, but she should be at school right now.

120
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:05,897
I'm worried about her.

121
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,152
She got through it last time too.

122
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:15,448
She'll be okay.

123
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:23,498
I'm so scared
she might do something to herself.

124
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:25,333
Jieun.

125
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,836
Jisun isn't that weak.

126
00:10:28,837 --> 00:10:30,046
She'll be fine.

127
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,051
She's not answering.

128
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:22,807
- Jisun!
-  Jisun!

129
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,434
What happened? Are you okay?

130
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:28,770
Hey, you're…
You're going to catch a cold.

131
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:30,690
- Let's get you inside.
-  I'm…

132
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,568
I'm hungry.

133
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:36,278
Okay,
let's get you something to eat.

134
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,779
-  Man…
-  Let's go inside.

135
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,782
How did you get so soaked?

136
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:56,966
When you're surfing…

137
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,471
the place where you start
is called the lineup.

138
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:06,517
But on the way out there,
wave after wave keeps coming at you.

139
00:12:12,941 --> 00:12:15,485
<i>Whether you go over them or around them…</i>

140
00:12:16,778 --> 00:12:19,239
<i>…you have to make it through
to reach the lineup.</i>

141
00:12:22,784 --> 00:12:24,118
<i>Getting to the starting point…</i>

142
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:28,790
<i>might be the hardest part of surfing.</i>

143
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,381
Earlier, I really wanted to die.

144
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:51,145
All kinds of thoughts came to me
together with the waves.

145
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:55,650
<i>"Should I run away?"</i>

146
00:12:56,651 --> 00:12:58,152
<i>"Should I just die?"</i>

147
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,575
<i>"If I make it through those waves,</i>

148
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:08,288
<i>will I be able to get back
to the starting point?"</i>

149
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:23,428
Even though I knew
the waves would probably sweep me away.

150
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:37,984
What about the school?

151
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,278
Haven't they said anything?

152
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:44,157
I didn't do anything wrong, you know.

153
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,034
It's my job.

154
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:51,163
The foundation isn't going
to let this slide.

155
00:13:51,164 --> 00:13:54,792
If you're really dead-set on doing this,
you need to know what you're getting into.

156
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:58,587
What you've been through so far
will seem like nothing.

157
00:13:58,588 --> 00:14:01,381
The truth will get lost,
and only the controversy will remain.

158
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:03,926
But the truth always comes out eventually.

159
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,220
What if it doesn't?

160
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:13,394
It'll be better than
living like I'm already dead.

161
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:25,740
<i>Are you going to keep this up?</i>

162
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:34,832
I don't know whether I should scold you
or try to comfort you.

163
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:38,336
If there's anything you want to tell me,
go ahead.

164
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,798
And if there's anything you want to ask,
just ask.

165
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,303
There's someone at school
I can actually talk to now.

166
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:50,723
Who, Soyeon?

167
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:54,352
Ms. Kang Jisun.

168
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:02,318
Was it Ms. Kang?

169
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:07,490
What do you mean?

170
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,160
Did you do it with my teacher?

171
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:16,456
I said bad things about that woman
without knowing anything.

172
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,501
- But if it was Ms. Kang--
- It was Ms. Kang.

173
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:24,674
- Why didn't you tell me?
- I had no idea she'd be like that.

174
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:28,426
I kept quiet because of you, Hyunsoo.

175
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:31,805
She's your teacher, and I was worried
it might hurt you in some way.

176
00:15:31,806 --> 00:15:35,393
Even if people pointed fingers at me,
I couldn't let you suffer because of it.

177
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,523
So…

178
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:43,734
just keep going to school.

179
00:15:48,406 --> 00:15:49,614
No.

180
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:50,907
I don't want to.

181
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,118
I'm not going to school.

182
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:05,715
I saw the article.

183
00:16:09,552 --> 00:16:10,678
Do you believe me?

184
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:14,307
Yes.

185
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:16,851
Liar.

186
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:21,564
Some of it, at least.

187
00:16:24,442 --> 00:16:26,235
I'm not a gold digger.

188
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,492
And I'm not some
mentally unstable pathological liar.

189
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:38,122
I…

190
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:42,919
I didn't lie.

191
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:56,807
Remember your polygraph?

192
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:01,186
And…

193
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:02,687
you're the one who reported that

194
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,565
there were narcotics
at Min's house, right?

195
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:08,569
I don't know anything about that.

196
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,613
That's a lie.

197
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,949
I don't know how you knew,

198
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:17,328
but you even specified
that it was under the bed.

199
00:17:17,912 --> 00:17:21,206
Two vehicles and five police officers
were deployed for the search.

200
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:23,959
Do you know what you could face
for making a false report--

201
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,587
Well, I'm glad you were diligent
when it came to drugs.

202
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:33,678
You were painfully slow
when investigating my case.

203
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:44,855
Want one?

204
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:47,858
No.

205
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:58,327
I don't think the investigation
was entirely conclusive either.

206
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:03,499
The reason I wanted to meet with you…

207
00:18:06,294 --> 00:18:08,421
was to warn you…

208
00:18:11,299 --> 00:18:12,800
about Min Junho.

209
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:23,311
Wait, Detective.

210
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:27,481
If you're free,

211
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,484
would you like to get a drink with me?

212
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:41,579
You asked us to include a question

213
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:45,583
about Min Junho's late wife
in the polygraph test.

214
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:51,505
<i>We actually did include it.</i>

215
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:55,676
Did you love your wife?

216
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,220
DID YOU LOVE YOUR WIFE?

217
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,222
Yes.

218
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:06,062
What's your happiest memory
with your wife?

219
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:12,735
I'd have to say when our child was born.

220
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:18,574
Did you ever resent your wife

221
00:19:19,617 --> 00:19:21,661
for taking her own life?

222
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:24,705
No.

223
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:31,002
Did you feel guilty?

224
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:34,799
DID YOU FEEL GUILTY
ABOUT YOUR WIFE'S DEATH?

225
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:45,518
I loved my wife so much that
I respected the final choice she made.

226
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:54,860
She looked free from all the pain
she'd been living with.

227
00:19:57,822 --> 00:19:59,240
She looked at peace.

228
00:20:01,117 --> 00:20:05,079
<i>When his wife died of
respiratory failure from a drug overdose…</i>

229
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:09,458
<i>Min Junho was at home.</i>

230
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:17,425
If he had anything to do
with his wife's death…

231
00:20:19,552 --> 00:20:21,053
he's a very dangerous man.

232
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,557
Don't try to confront him.

233
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:27,768
Just stay as far away from him as you can.

234
00:20:30,271 --> 00:20:31,897
Why are you telling me all this?

235
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:38,070
It's not as a police officer…

236
00:20:41,115 --> 00:20:42,700
Just woman to woman.

237
00:20:45,327 --> 00:20:48,372
Officially, you're not supposed to be
telling me this, are you?

238
00:20:51,417 --> 00:20:53,461
Maybe it's the hormones.

239
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,297
I'm pregnant.

240
00:21:02,595 --> 00:21:04,555
It makes me think about the kind of world…

241
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:07,767
my child will grow up in.

242
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:15,441
If anything happens,
or if you ever need anything, call me.

243
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:57,858
Aren't you going to school?

244
00:22:00,486 --> 00:22:01,779
How did you find me here?

245
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:04,365
I looked for you.

246
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:06,909
You can never hide from me.

247
00:22:10,538 --> 00:22:11,914
Why aren't you going to school?

248
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:15,084
Why aren't you?

249
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:18,921
I put in for an experiential learning day.

250
00:22:19,964 --> 00:22:20,965
Why?

251
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:26,136
I barely passed the monthly evaluation,
so I need to practice.

252
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:29,723
My singing's fine,
but apparently my dancing needs work.

253
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,227
So annoying.

254
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:39,316
Want to team up with me
for the science project presentation?

255
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:41,735
You and me?

256
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:45,447
You're the best at science in our class.

257
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:48,659
I don't want to.

258
00:22:49,994 --> 00:22:50,995
Why not?

259
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:53,913
Do it with your boyfriend.

260
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,126
Who? Sanghyeon?

261
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:59,878
That's crazy.

262
00:22:59,879 --> 00:23:02,006
He just let me use his account
the most, okay?

263
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:04,967
That's why I'm just being nice to him.

264
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:09,346
Besides, I already have a boyfriend.

265
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:13,392
You.

266
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:18,522
What?

267
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:20,149
You don't want to be?

268
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:25,446
You're kind of a loser
at everything except studying.

269
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:28,615
And I'm only a loser
when it comes to studying.

270
00:23:28,616 --> 00:23:30,367
Losers should stick together.

271
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:32,745
Deal?

272
00:23:35,456 --> 00:23:38,834
And I don't care at all
about what happened with your dad.

273
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:42,838
I don't even care
what my own dad is up to.

274
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:56,976
Hello.

275
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:58,186
Hi.

276
00:23:58,187 --> 00:24:00,605
-  Hey, it's the gold digger.
-  Don't make eye contact.

277
00:24:00,606 --> 00:24:02,106
She really has no shame.

278
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:03,274
But is that story true?

279
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:04,359
-  I wonder too.
- Hello.

280
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,027
-  Isn't that insane?
-  I know.

281
00:24:06,028 --> 00:24:07,696
Hello.

282
00:24:08,364 --> 00:24:10,990
You think she became a teacher
to extort money from people?

283
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:13,577
Wow, so embarrassing.

284
00:24:14,995 --> 00:24:16,621
Hey,
it's the gold-digger teacher.

285
00:24:16,622 --> 00:24:19,833
She gives me the creeps.
Why's she here? Wasn't she fired?

286
00:24:21,043 --> 00:24:24,004
What's this going to do
to our school's reputation?

287
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:28,299
Our priority is keeping
the students from getting worked up,

288
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,343
especially with midterms coming up…

289
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:31,595
I'm sorry I'm late.

290
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:34,431
Ms. Kang Jisun?

291
00:24:35,516 --> 00:24:36,725
Spare me a minute.

292
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:47,653
Do you think you can show up to school
whenever you feel like it?

293
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:49,530
I'm sorry.

294
00:24:50,072 --> 00:24:52,365
You know how much the parents complain,
don't you?

295
00:24:52,366 --> 00:24:55,618
When it comes to their kids,
they scrutinize every little thing,

296
00:24:55,619 --> 00:24:56,996
and then gossip about it.

297
00:24:57,997 --> 00:25:00,248
Haven't you ever wondered

298
00:25:00,249 --> 00:25:03,252
whether you really belong
at Sangcheon's top private school?

299
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:08,674
Pardon me?

300
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:14,053
The school board has agreed
that they simply can't overlook a teacher

301
00:25:14,054 --> 00:25:16,432
who has disgraced the school's name.

302
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:22,021
I've disgraced the school's name?

303
00:25:26,567 --> 00:25:28,985
- I find that hard to accept--
- Everyone's up in arms,

304
00:25:28,986 --> 00:25:30,737
saying you made baseless accusations

305
00:25:30,738 --> 00:25:34,324
and damaged the reputation
of a highly successful man!

306
00:25:35,701 --> 00:25:37,201
And it's not just Dr. Min.

307
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:40,539
Hyunsoo is at one of
the most important stages of his life.

308
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:49,214
What about me?

309
00:25:53,093 --> 00:25:54,303
What about my life?

310
00:25:59,433 --> 00:26:01,934
Get it sorted out
before it becomes a bigger issue.

311
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:03,520
You know what I mean, right?

312
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:40,974
I'm the victim.

313
00:26:45,229 --> 00:26:47,231
That's why I filed a complaint, but…

314
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:51,860
the accused was released
due to insufficient evidence.

315
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:00,284
I've requested a reinvestigation,

316
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:02,663
and I believe his side
leaked the story to the press.

317
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:09,962
The article is clearly false,

318
00:27:10,838 --> 00:27:12,756
and I'm going to demand a correction.

319
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:23,350
I'm going to see this through
until the truth comes out.

320
00:27:25,102 --> 00:27:28,605
That's the only way
I can face my students without shame.

321
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:31,900
Ms. Kang, you…

322
00:27:34,194 --> 00:27:37,990
You've violated your duty to maintain
the dignity expected of a teacher.

323
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:42,785
How is that…

324
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:44,371
It's a matter of personal privacy.

325
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:47,124
So it's not my place to get involved.

326
00:27:48,250 --> 00:27:53,672
And whether the article is true
isn't really the issue.

327
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,884
If the truth doesn't matter,
then what does?

328
00:27:58,719 --> 00:28:00,345
It was written with malicious intent.

329
00:28:02,347 --> 00:28:04,223
It's just something that's going around,

330
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:06,435
so I don't know
how much of it to believe, but…

331
00:28:07,603 --> 00:28:08,770
they say the man…

332
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:13,609
was Min Hyunsoo's father.

333
00:28:20,657 --> 00:28:21,658
That…

334
00:28:24,912 --> 00:28:27,623
did not violate any professional ethics.

335
00:28:30,876 --> 00:28:34,503
If you don't see anything wrong

336
00:28:34,504 --> 00:28:37,132
with a teacher
getting personally involved…

337
00:28:40,052 --> 00:28:42,095
with a student's parent,

338
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:44,681
that's even more of a problem.

339
00:28:51,647 --> 00:28:53,899
Was it Dr. Min Junho?

340
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,281
Yes.

341
00:29:09,706 --> 00:29:11,833
I think it'd be best
to take a leave of absence.

342
00:29:12,626 --> 00:29:16,420
Of course,
we could convene a disciplinary committee…

343
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:20,883
…but putting you through
something like that

344
00:29:20,884 --> 00:29:23,387
wouldn't do you any good either.

345
00:29:25,347 --> 00:29:27,349
Your teacher evaluations have been good.

346
00:29:28,266 --> 00:29:34,272
And I appreciate how hard
you've worked for the students.

347
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:40,737
Rather than the school
putting you on leave,

348
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:44,616
I think it'd be better
if you requested one.

349
00:29:52,332 --> 00:29:53,792
Ms. Kang Jisun.

350
00:29:56,712 --> 00:29:58,797
A teacher who stands in front of students

351
00:29:59,589 --> 00:30:01,425
can't fall apart so easily,

352
00:30:02,426 --> 00:30:03,927
no matter the reason.

353
00:30:25,699 --> 00:30:27,284
<i>You're finished now.</i>

354
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:47,928
YOU'RE FINISHED NOW!

355
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:49,056
<i>Who are you?</i>

356
00:30:56,188 --> 00:30:58,398
<i>Someone who knows you very well.</i>

357
00:31:26,802 --> 00:31:33,558
TO MS. KANG JISUN
FROM KIM RIAN

358
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:15,600
Stop it.

359
00:33:06,568 --> 00:33:08,028
Why did you do that to my dad?

360
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:13,116
What?

361
00:33:14,117 --> 00:33:15,660
Was it really for money?

362
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:21,040
Did your dad say that?

363
00:33:21,041 --> 00:33:23,126
Even after everything,
he said you were a good person.

364
00:33:25,879 --> 00:33:27,630
I want to be a good person.

365
00:33:27,631 --> 00:33:29,299
I've always tried to live that way.

366
00:33:30,759 --> 00:33:31,926
But your dad really--

367
00:33:31,927 --> 00:33:32,928
My dad, what?

368
00:33:40,352 --> 00:33:43,520
I want to tell you I'm sorry,
but I don't know if I should.

369
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:44,980
You should apologize to my dad.

370
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:47,609
No. I don't owe your dad an apology.

371
00:33:54,699 --> 00:33:58,035
I can't explain how things got to this,

372
00:33:58,036 --> 00:33:59,871
but I didn't lie.

373
00:34:09,214 --> 00:34:10,507
Hyunsoo.

374
00:34:11,508 --> 00:34:12,509
Are you okay?

375
00:34:14,552 --> 00:34:15,971
Don't pretend you care.

376
00:34:30,443 --> 00:34:31,777
Yes?

377
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:33,612
PRINCIPAL JEONG SANGYEONG

378
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:34,614
-  Hello.
- Ah.

379
00:34:37,951 --> 00:34:38,952
Hello.

380
00:34:39,786 --> 00:34:43,289
Oh, yes. You came all the way out here.

381
00:34:43,290 --> 00:34:44,582
SANGCHEON MEDIA
OH DAESIK

382
00:34:46,835 --> 00:34:50,170
I'd like to dig a little deeper
into what happened at the time.

383
00:34:50,171 --> 00:34:53,173
I was thinking there might be enough
for an in-depth piece.

384
00:34:53,174 --> 00:34:56,928
Well, I've read the article
and even done a phone interview,

385
00:34:57,512 --> 00:35:01,223
but I can't help wondering if it's right
to keep digging into something like this.

386
00:35:01,224 --> 00:35:05,144
It's been keeping me up at night
and bothering me.

387
00:35:05,145 --> 00:35:07,314
Fighting injustice is never easy.

388
00:35:08,023 --> 00:35:11,442
But the longer people stay silent,
the more victims there will be.

389
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:12,944
Exactly.

390
00:35:13,486 --> 00:35:16,697
The world has changed so much
from the way it used to be.

391
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:20,284
I heard you went through
quite an ordeal back then.

392
00:35:20,285 --> 00:35:22,370
It was a difficult time.

393
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:25,706
In my 36 years as an educator,

394
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:27,792
nothing like that
had ever happened before.

395
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:32,130
Anyway, I decided it was all
due to my own shortcomings,

396
00:35:32,839 --> 00:35:34,632
so I forgave her and put it behind me.

397
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:35,634
Hmm…

398
00:35:37,218 --> 00:35:43,682
So Ms. Kang Jisun falsely accused you
of demanding sexual favors from her

399
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:46,560
and even sexually harassing her,

400
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:47,978
and you forgave her?

401
00:35:47,979 --> 00:35:52,524
She really went too far,
accusing me of something like that.

402
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:55,444
I was so dumbfounded and felt so wronged

403
00:35:55,445 --> 00:35:57,780
that I had security cameras
installed afterward.

404
00:35:57,781 --> 00:36:00,617
Look. I had two of them installed.

405
00:36:03,370 --> 00:36:05,872
So none of that ever happened?

406
00:36:06,623 --> 00:36:08,375
Of course not.

407
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:11,335
I thought of her like a daughter.

408
00:36:11,336 --> 00:36:13,128
No, don't get the wrong idea.

409
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:15,215
She's actually an old friend's daughter.

410
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:17,342
Really?

411
00:36:17,926 --> 00:36:20,094
Her father died young,

412
00:36:20,095 --> 00:36:22,013
so I knew she'd had
a hard time growing up.

413
00:36:23,348 --> 00:36:27,727
I hired her as a contract teacher
for my late friend's sake.

414
00:36:28,311 --> 00:36:30,480
Then, about a year later,

415
00:36:31,147 --> 00:36:34,609
they told us to replace
all contract teachers with permanent ones.

416
00:36:35,276 --> 00:36:38,321
Anyway, she heard about it
and came to see me.

417
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:44,869
Ms. Kang.

418
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:51,376
I think we'll have to let you go
at the end of this month.

419
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:56,047
You're very popular with the students,

420
00:36:56,715 --> 00:36:59,801
and they did well
in the last academic competition too.

421
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:03,972
But I'm sorry it had to come to this.

422
00:37:04,848 --> 00:37:06,182
Exactly, sir.

423
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:09,810
I got all my students to place
in the competition.

424
00:37:09,811 --> 00:37:11,937
How can you just
let me go all of a sudden?

425
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:16,568
The foundation wants us rated
as an outstanding educational institution,

426
00:37:17,068 --> 00:37:19,153
so all our teachers have to be full-time.

427
00:37:19,154 --> 00:37:20,905
That's the policy they handed down.

428
00:37:24,159 --> 00:37:27,161
But you could put in
a good word for me, sir.

429
00:37:27,162 --> 00:37:28,329
Can't you do that for me?

430
00:37:30,540 --> 00:37:34,294
You know I think of you
like a daughter, right?

431
00:37:34,878 --> 00:37:37,547
And you know I think of you
like a father, right?

432
00:37:39,007 --> 00:37:42,135
You should take the certification exam
and get a job at a public school.

433
00:37:43,511 --> 00:37:45,263
Are you really going to do this to me?

434
00:37:45,889 --> 00:37:48,140
I'm saying this for your own good.

435
00:37:48,141 --> 00:37:51,685
If you want what's best for me,
you should pull some strings for me.

436
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:54,271
There's nothing I can do
about the foundation's decision.

437
00:37:54,272 --> 00:37:56,441
What could I possibly do?

438
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:09,661
Then the next day,
I got a call from the police.

439
00:38:09,662 --> 00:38:10,663
She told them

440
00:38:11,748 --> 00:38:13,750
that I tried to do something to her.

441
00:38:15,001 --> 00:38:16,835
Even though you didn't do anything?

442
00:38:16,836 --> 00:38:19,129
How could I ever think of her that way?

443
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:21,632
I've known her since she was a kid.

444
00:38:21,633 --> 00:38:24,593
I don't even want to think about
what happened after that.

445
00:38:24,594 --> 00:38:26,053
It was a living hell.

446
00:38:26,054 --> 00:38:28,973
Everyone got the wrong idea,
and nasty rumors went around.

447
00:38:29,808 --> 00:38:32,852
I haven't told anyone before,
but I thought about taking my own life.

448
00:38:34,062 --> 00:38:36,856
Then why did you pay her a settlement?

449
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:38,733
A settlement?

450
00:38:39,776 --> 00:38:41,026
I never paid her anything.

451
00:38:41,027 --> 00:38:44,613
The police said she dropped the charges
after receiving a settlement.

452
00:38:44,614 --> 00:38:46,323
Oh, no, that's not what happened.

453
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:48,033
She has an older sister, Jieun.

454
00:38:48,034 --> 00:38:50,869
Her sister made a scene,
asking how she could be doing this

455
00:38:50,870 --> 00:38:52,580
and told her to drop the charges.

456
00:38:53,289 --> 00:38:55,792
I was just about to be cleared,
by the way.

457
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:59,963
Then, Jieun came and got on her knees,
begging for forgiveness.

458
00:39:01,005 --> 00:39:04,259
I felt bad for her,
so I gave five million won as severance.

459
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:07,761
As severance pay, not a settlement?

460
00:39:07,762 --> 00:39:08,846
Yes.

461
00:39:08,847 --> 00:39:12,057
She was still my friend's daughter,
so I couldn't help but feel for her.

462
00:39:12,058 --> 00:39:14,101
Though later,

463
00:39:14,102 --> 00:39:16,603
I thought maybe
I shouldn't have done that either.

464
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:17,605
Why's that?

465
00:39:18,898 --> 00:39:21,860
Well, I'd rather not dig up things
from her past if I don't have to.

466
00:39:22,944 --> 00:39:25,446
Her? Who do you mean? Ms. Kang Jisun?

467
00:39:29,701 --> 00:39:31,618
Well, since we're on the subject…

468
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:32,620
Take a look at this.

469
00:39:33,496 --> 00:39:35,622
A parent took this photo
and shared it with me.

470
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:39,626
They work at this hotel,
and apparently she frequents this place.

471
00:39:39,627 --> 00:39:41,962
You know, the place that was on the news

472
00:39:41,963 --> 00:39:45,173
for young people drinking,
dancing, and partying it up.

473
00:39:45,174 --> 00:39:47,426
- What do you call it?
- A nightclub.

474
00:39:47,427 --> 00:39:48,552
- A club.
- Yes.

475
00:39:48,553 --> 00:39:49,887
Apparently she's a regular.

476
00:39:49,888 --> 00:39:51,889
They ran into her several times.

477
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:55,642
They said they took the photo
to complain to the school

478
00:39:55,643 --> 00:39:57,936
about hiring someone like her
as a teacher,

479
00:39:57,937 --> 00:39:59,314
regardless of her private life.

480
00:40:02,775 --> 00:40:04,067
This photo…

481
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:05,361
Could you send it to me?

482
00:40:33,514 --> 00:40:36,808
<i>You really are
the man who protects hearts.</i>

483
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:39,019
<i>Now, for my final question.</i>

484
00:40:39,020 --> 00:40:42,731
<i>When does the heart pound the most?</i>

485
00:40:42,732 --> 00:40:44,442
<i>Is it when we're in danger?</i>

486
00:40:45,193 --> 00:40:47,236
<i>You see, the heart…</i>

487
00:40:48,529 --> 00:40:49,781
<i>It actually pounds more</i>

488
00:40:50,782 --> 00:40:53,284
<i>when you're lying
than when you're in danger.</i>

489
00:40:55,912 --> 00:40:58,998
<i>So for your heart's sake, try not to lie.</i>

490
00:41:13,763 --> 00:41:15,765
<i>Can a party girl really be a teacher?</i>

491
00:41:27,902 --> 00:41:30,237
ACCUSED MAN'S LIFE IN RUINS,
ACCUSER HITS THE CLUBS

492
00:41:30,238 --> 00:41:31,239
REPORTER OH DAESIK

493
00:41:38,788 --> 00:41:40,288
YOUR LIFE IS OVER NOW.
SERVES YOU RIGHT.

494
00:41:40,289 --> 00:41:41,457
YOUR FATHER WOULD BE SO PROUD.

495
00:41:43,626 --> 00:41:45,420
<i>Your life is over now.</i>

496
00:41:45,962 --> 00:41:47,671
<i>Serves you right.</i>

497
00:41:47,672 --> 00:41:49,924
<i>Your father would be so proud.</i>

498
00:42:19,620 --> 00:42:21,121
Well, well.

499
00:42:21,122 --> 00:42:22,539
To what do I owe the pleasure?

500
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:24,249
Why are you doing this to me?

501
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:26,251
This has nothing to do with you.

502
00:42:26,252 --> 00:42:28,921
He ended up your victim just like I did.

503
00:42:29,881 --> 00:42:32,007
It's time you fixed
that nasty habit of yours,

504
00:42:32,008 --> 00:42:35,594
leading men on,
then stabbing them in the back.

505
00:42:35,595 --> 00:42:37,429
I dropped the charges.

506
00:42:37,430 --> 00:42:39,182
Everyone told me not to, but I did.

507
00:42:39,766 --> 00:42:41,933
<i>I gave you a chance,</i>

508
00:42:41,934 --> 00:42:43,643
and that's how you repay me?

509
00:42:43,644 --> 00:42:46,521
I got that job on my own!

510
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:51,151
You wouldn't have
gotten that job without me.

511
00:42:51,152 --> 00:42:53,654
Did you think everything
would come that easy?

512
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:56,990
You give a little, you get a little.

513
00:42:56,991 --> 00:42:58,451
<i>That's only fair!</i>

514
00:43:00,495 --> 00:43:01,662
You people…

515
00:43:03,206 --> 00:43:05,458
You haven't changed at all.

516
00:43:07,043 --> 00:43:08,210
And you never will.

517
00:43:10,421 --> 00:43:12,048
You little…

518
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:19,263
What the hell?

519
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:21,641
You gave them that photo, didn't you?

520
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:23,809
Why, you little…

521
00:43:23,810 --> 00:43:26,269
Show some respect to your father's friend!

522
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:27,897
If you don't want another fight,

523
00:43:28,648 --> 00:43:30,483
call that reporter.

524
00:43:31,567 --> 00:43:34,529
Tell them what you did
and how you covered it up.

525
00:43:35,404 --> 00:43:36,572
For crying out loud.

526
00:43:38,324 --> 00:43:41,202
If you're here to ask for a favor,
you should ask nicely.

527
00:43:43,913 --> 00:43:46,833
Or give me a little something in return.

528
00:43:57,301 --> 00:43:59,887
Do you want to keep teaching?

529
00:44:01,013 --> 00:44:02,348
Oh, yes.

530
00:44:15,528 --> 00:44:18,281
Then ask nicely.

531
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:26,205
Or give me a little something in return.

532
00:44:40,386 --> 00:44:44,681
Look at that. Just walking off
without even saying goodbye.

533
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:46,601
That rude little…

534
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:50,645
Hey, what are you doing?

535
00:44:53,065 --> 00:44:55,484
Stay out of my life from now on…

536
00:44:59,405 --> 00:45:01,157
…or you'll have to face my father

537
00:45:02,867 --> 00:45:05,870
and beg him for forgiveness on your knees.

538
00:45:18,549 --> 00:45:22,385
DETECTIVE LEE HWAYOUNG

539
00:45:22,386 --> 00:45:24,263
-  <i>Yes, Ms. Kang?</i>
- Jeong Sangyeong.

540
00:45:25,514 --> 00:45:29,226
He's the reason
the polygraph said I was lying.

541
00:45:29,227 --> 00:45:31,270
I was afraid they'd think
I did it habitually.

542
00:45:38,653 --> 00:45:42,073
<i>Have you ever
reported a sex crime before?</i>

543
00:45:47,078 --> 00:45:49,163
No, I have not.

544
00:46:02,343 --> 00:46:04,136
Damn it.

545
00:46:07,848 --> 00:46:10,767
BAEK HANUI'S QUESTION MARK

546
00:46:10,768 --> 00:46:12,728
VIEWER MESSAGE BOARD

547
00:46:14,855 --> 00:46:16,399
WRITE A POST

548
00:46:19,735 --> 00:46:21,152
<i>Min Junho,</i>

549
00:46:21,153 --> 00:46:23,989
<i>no matter how convincing a mask you wear,</i>

550
00:46:23,990 --> 00:46:25,783
<i>you're still a sex offender.</i>

551
00:46:48,431 --> 00:46:50,473
ORIGINAL POST
EXPOSING STAR DOCTOR

552
00:46:50,474 --> 00:46:54,561
<i>I am Kang Jisun, a teacher
at Sangcheon Haeon Elementary School.</i>

553
00:46:54,562 --> 00:46:57,188
<i>I was recently accused
of being a gold digger.</i>

554
00:46:57,189 --> 00:46:58,566
Hey, have you seen this post?

555
00:46:59,442 --> 00:47:04,404
<i>I'm writing this publicly
because I want the truth to come out.</i>

556
00:47:04,405 --> 00:47:06,740
-  Did you see this?
-  Yeah, what's this about?

557
00:47:06,741 --> 00:47:09,994
<i>Min Junho is a sex offender</i>

558
00:47:10,786 --> 00:47:14,540
<i>hiding behind the mask of a brilliant
cardiovascular surgeon and a good father.</i>

559
00:47:15,583 --> 00:47:17,625
<i>From now on,</i>

560
00:47:17,626 --> 00:47:19,879
<i>the whole world
will come to know who he really is.</i>

561
00:47:26,344 --> 00:47:28,803
<i>There's something I want to say to him.</i>

562
00:47:28,804 --> 00:47:30,056
Hyunsoo.

563
00:47:31,265 --> 00:47:32,350
What are you doing?

564
00:47:34,143 --> 00:47:37,063
<i>Min Junho, now it's your turn to suffer.</i>

565
00:47:48,199 --> 00:47:49,908
EXPOSÉ POSTED
ON VIEWER MESSAGE BOARD

566
00:47:49,909 --> 00:47:51,869
UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
CARDIOVASCULAR SURGEON

567
00:48:00,836 --> 00:48:02,630
How can you show your face at school?

568
00:48:03,464 --> 00:48:05,131
Son of a criminal.

569
00:48:05,132 --> 00:48:07,258
- It's disgusting.
- Shut up.

570
00:48:07,259 --> 00:48:10,637
Your dad did something to our teacher.
The whole school knows now.

571
00:48:10,638 --> 00:48:12,555
Damn it, what do you even know?

572
00:48:12,556 --> 00:48:14,808
Are you freaking crazy?

573
00:48:14,809 --> 00:48:16,351
Damn you!

574
00:48:16,352 --> 00:48:17,520
Get lost!

575
00:48:18,771 --> 00:48:20,314
-  Damn it.
-  Hey!

576
00:48:20,815 --> 00:48:23,441
What do you think you're doing?

577
00:48:23,442 --> 00:48:24,819
Hey! Hey!

578
00:48:27,488 --> 00:48:30,157
Here, let me see you.

579
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:39,999
Yes?

580
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:43,420
<i>Dr. Min, did you postpone Yunji's surgery?</i>

581
00:48:43,421 --> 00:48:45,756
No. Her surgery is tomorrow.

582
00:48:48,592 --> 00:48:49,677
Yes.

583
00:48:52,847 --> 00:48:56,517
Ma'am, you didn't give Yunji
any chocolate today, did you?

584
00:48:57,226 --> 00:48:58,561
Dr. Min.

585
00:49:04,150 --> 00:49:06,902
Is something wrong?

586
00:49:09,113 --> 00:49:10,114
Did you…

587
00:49:11,115 --> 00:49:12,782
postpone the surgery because…

588
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:13,867
I didn't postpone it.

589
00:49:13,868 --> 00:49:16,245
I asked for a different doctor.

590
00:49:17,746 --> 00:49:20,416
I can't entrust my child
to a sex offender.

591
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:27,005
I clearly asked for a different doctor,

592
00:49:27,006 --> 00:49:29,507
so if he keeps coming in
whenever he pleases,

593
00:49:29,508 --> 00:49:31,343
we'll have to change hospitals.

594
00:49:31,886 --> 00:49:34,889
Ma'am, there's been a misunderstanding.

595
00:49:37,183 --> 00:49:38,808
Yunji's life is at stake.

596
00:49:38,809 --> 00:49:42,104
- We need to go ahead with the surgery--
- I decide what's best for my child.

597
00:49:43,481 --> 00:49:45,482
To think she was in your care
this whole time.

598
00:49:45,483 --> 00:49:46,983
- Ma'am…
-  Dr. Min.

599
00:49:46,984 --> 00:49:48,944
I didn't get a chance to tell you.

600
00:49:49,737 --> 00:49:52,447
The well-being of the patient
and guardian comes first,

601
00:49:52,448 --> 00:49:54,574
so please step outside for now.

602
00:50:10,966 --> 00:50:12,050
Hello?

603
00:50:12,051 --> 00:50:13,969
<i>Am I speaking with Hyunsoo's father?</i>

604
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:21,519
Oh, Mr. Min.

605
00:50:24,230 --> 00:50:25,313
What happened?

606
00:50:25,314 --> 00:50:28,358
The CT results are normal.
It's just a minor head injury.

607
00:50:28,359 --> 00:50:30,694
We put in six stitches,
and we're almost done.

608
00:50:32,071 --> 00:50:34,156
Mr. Min, I sincerely apologize.

609
00:50:34,823 --> 00:50:40,246
I'll make sure the students who hurt him
receive appropriate disciplinary action.

610
00:50:41,914 --> 00:50:43,249
Who did this to you?

611
00:50:44,291 --> 00:50:45,667
Can't we just let it go?

612
00:50:45,668 --> 00:50:47,753
We can't just let violence slide.

613
00:50:48,671 --> 00:50:50,755
Tell me. Are you going to tell me or not?

614
00:50:50,756 --> 00:50:52,383
Have you always done the right thing?

615
00:51:05,771 --> 00:51:07,439
What exactly do you want from me?

616
00:51:09,149 --> 00:51:10,234
The truth.

617
00:51:10,985 --> 00:51:13,319
Please, just stop
with those ridiculous lies!

618
00:51:13,320 --> 00:51:16,364
I can't stop because they're not lies.

619
00:51:16,365 --> 00:51:20,076
Do you have any idea what my son
and I are going through because of you?

620
00:51:20,077 --> 00:51:22,663
That's not because of me.
It's because of you.

621
00:51:23,455 --> 00:51:26,709
If you hadn't done that to me,
none of this would've happened.

622
00:51:29,628 --> 00:51:33,966
By now, you would've been planning
to make a nice sum off me.

623
00:51:35,593 --> 00:51:37,427
Is this because that didn't work out?

624
00:51:37,428 --> 00:51:39,555
You drugged my wine.

625
00:51:41,015 --> 00:51:43,017
You thought I'd never find out,
didn't you?

626
00:51:43,642 --> 00:51:46,186
If you've done something wrong,
you have to pay the price!

627
00:51:58,657 --> 00:52:01,159
Sue her for false accusation
and defamation right away.

628
00:52:01,160 --> 00:52:03,662
You need to be firm
for Hyunsoo to hold his head up high.

629
00:52:06,874 --> 00:52:09,418
I'll never understand some people.

630
00:52:10,002 --> 00:52:12,587
Hey, I know that better than anyone, okay?

631
00:52:12,588 --> 00:52:15,466
You can never forgive a woman like that.
What's the law there for?

632
00:52:37,738 --> 00:52:39,198
What the…

633
00:52:43,285 --> 00:52:45,287
Oh, my gosh!

634
00:52:47,539 --> 00:52:49,165
Jieun…

635
00:52:49,166 --> 00:52:50,459
Goodness.

636
00:52:52,628 --> 00:52:55,213
Your phone was off, so…

637
00:52:55,214 --> 00:52:57,633
Gosh, Jieun…

638
00:53:06,433 --> 00:53:10,020
It's because I gave up
instead of fighting to the end back then.

639
00:53:13,023 --> 00:53:14,608
So now…

640
00:53:16,568 --> 00:53:20,072
it came back like a boomerang
and turned me into a liar.

641
00:53:23,992 --> 00:53:25,327
Because of that…

642
00:53:26,620 --> 00:53:29,456
I've lost everything
I've achieved up until now.

643
00:53:34,378 --> 00:53:36,880
Jisun, do you want one too?

644
00:53:37,798 --> 00:53:40,717
I shouldn't have accepted the money
from the principal back then.

645
00:53:42,302 --> 00:53:43,554
It's okay.

646
00:53:45,389 --> 00:53:48,475
You were fooled
by that sly old bastard too.

647
00:53:49,601 --> 00:53:52,521
You said he lied and said
it was money he had borrowed from Dad.

648
00:53:54,273 --> 00:53:55,858
We were too naive.

649
00:53:56,358 --> 00:53:57,984
Neither of you did anything wrong.

650
00:53:57,985 --> 00:54:00,237
Those bastards are the ones to blame.

651
00:54:00,821 --> 00:54:04,241
Let's focus on getting you a job first.

652
00:54:05,117 --> 00:54:07,786
Yeah, you can do anything, Jisun.

653
00:54:12,916 --> 00:54:14,418
I will…

654
00:54:17,171 --> 00:54:18,922
uncover the truth at all costs

655
00:54:20,382 --> 00:54:22,634
and put everything back the way it was.

656
00:54:29,975 --> 00:54:30,976
Jisun.

657
00:54:32,144 --> 00:54:33,228
I get what you're saying.

658
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:36,647
I totally agree with you.

659
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:38,024
But…

660
00:54:38,025 --> 00:54:39,985
how are you going to uncover the truth?

661
00:54:50,579 --> 00:54:51,663
I don't know.

662
00:54:56,084 --> 00:54:57,836
I don't know yet either.

663
00:55:10,474 --> 00:55:11,891
Thanks to the article,

664
00:55:11,892 --> 00:55:14,895
the post you wrote
is getting tons of views.

665
00:55:17,648 --> 00:55:18,732
I know.

666
00:55:20,734 --> 00:55:23,028
I also know what everyone's saying.

667
00:55:26,657 --> 00:55:30,034
"Serial gold digger
after settlement money."

668
00:55:30,035 --> 00:55:31,619
"He's too good for her."

669
00:55:31,620 --> 00:55:33,121
"Pathological liar."

670
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:39,962
You shouldn't have posted it
on social media under your real name.

671
00:55:40,963 --> 00:55:42,630
If there are people supporting you,

672
00:55:42,631 --> 00:55:45,592
there are bound to be people
criticizing and attacking you too.

673
00:55:46,885 --> 00:55:50,013
I can't even have him punished,
and you're telling me to stay quiet?

674
00:55:51,014 --> 00:55:54,725
They've already branded me promiscuous.
What good would keeping quiet do?

675
00:55:54,726 --> 00:55:57,271
I'm just worried about you.

676
00:55:58,897 --> 00:56:01,400
You can't keep starting over.

677
00:56:05,612 --> 00:56:08,114
I'm going to rethink everything
from the beginning.

678
00:56:08,115 --> 00:56:09,366
From the very beginning.

679
00:56:31,763 --> 00:56:34,099
<i>Jisun, did you go somewhere?</i>

680
00:56:34,850 --> 00:56:35,851
<i>Jieun.</i>

681
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:39,271
<i>What happened that day
might have been planned from the start.</i>

682
00:56:40,939 --> 00:56:43,859
<i>Maybe I wasn't Min Junho's first victim.</i>

683
00:56:45,277 --> 00:56:46,612
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

684
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:51,199
<i>This time,
I'm not stopping halfway.</i>

685
00:56:52,200 --> 00:56:54,786
<i>I'm going to find out
exactly who he really is.</i>

686
00:56:55,996 --> 00:56:57,456
<i>Where are you now?</i>

687
00:57:03,420 --> 00:57:05,172
Defamation and false accusation?

688
00:57:09,051 --> 00:57:11,887
My lawyer friend offered
to file the complaint for me,

689
00:57:12,929 --> 00:57:15,474
but I'm still not sure.

690
00:57:17,225 --> 00:57:19,769
And there were a few things
I wanted to ask you,

691
00:57:19,770 --> 00:57:20,854
so I came in person.

692
00:57:22,147 --> 00:57:23,148
Go ahead.

693
00:57:29,571 --> 00:57:33,407
I was reported for a drug offense
and investigated--

694
00:57:33,408 --> 00:57:34,826
I know.

695
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:44,126
The police came into my house,
didn't search anywhere else,

696
00:57:44,127 --> 00:57:46,879
and went straight for
the vials under my bed.

697
00:57:46,880 --> 00:57:48,382
I know that too.

698
00:57:56,598 --> 00:57:58,600
What else do you know?

699
00:58:01,061 --> 00:58:02,312
That's all.

700
00:58:08,777 --> 00:58:11,780
It looks like someone broke into my house.

701
00:58:12,614 --> 00:58:14,449
I checked the security cameras too.

702
00:58:14,991 --> 00:58:17,827
You can't really see her face,
but it's definitely a woman.

703
00:58:17,828 --> 00:58:19,496
Are you going to report it?

704
00:58:23,583 --> 00:58:24,793
If I do, can you find her?

705
00:58:25,293 --> 00:58:26,962
File a report first, then we can talk.

706
00:58:28,922 --> 00:58:31,550
And I don't handle defamation
or false accusation cases.

707
00:58:52,195 --> 00:58:55,824
Thank you for all your help until now.

708
00:58:57,033 --> 00:58:58,118
Goodbye.

709
00:59:21,808 --> 00:59:23,226
I'll see you again.

710
00:59:46,249 --> 00:59:48,292
<i>In a moment, you'll enter</i>

711
00:59:48,293 --> 00:59:50,378
<i>a 60-kilometer-per-hour
speed enforcement zone.</i>

712
01:01:00,907 --> 01:01:02,992
SATURDAY, SUNDAY

713
01:01:02,993 --> 01:01:04,160
 Hey, it's me.

714
01:01:04,744 --> 01:01:06,579
I need you to run a plate for me.

715
01:01:06,580 --> 01:01:08,665
It's 182P 1905.

716
01:01:09,666 --> 01:01:12,252
Yeah, I just need
the registered owner's name.

717
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:14,421
Get it to me as soon as you can.

718
01:01:15,672 --> 01:01:16,673
Thanks.

719
01:03:02,570 --> 01:03:06,950
MY HUSBAND

720
01:03:46,656 --> 01:03:50,577
THE PERFECT LIE

721
01:04:16,936 --> 01:04:20,148
 <i>You can't believe Min Junho
would do something like that, can you?</i>

722
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:24,319
I hope you can go to the police
and tell them the truth,

723
01:04:24,903 --> 01:04:28,739
and let people know
what kind of person Min Junho really is.

724
01:04:28,740 --> 01:04:32,284
 <i>You're only making things worse
for yourself by doing this here.</i>

725
01:04:32,285 --> 01:04:34,161
 <i>Did you find out
who the car is registered to?</i>

726
01:04:34,162 --> 01:04:36,080
<i>I'll give you a chance to start over.</i>

727
01:04:36,081 --> 01:04:37,748
<i>How about we share a bottle of wine?</i>

728
01:04:37,749 --> 01:04:38,999
Wait! Hey.

729
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:42,128
With sincere remorse and an apology.

730
01:04:43,797 --> 01:04:45,339
<i>You win.</i>

731
01:05:01,147 --> 01:05:02,815
THE PERFECT LIE

732
01:05:02,816 --> 01:05:04,818
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
